    {
      "type": "generalise",
      "difficulty": 2,
      "prose": "Every time, you multiplied by the same factor once per step. A change of $r$ per step, as a decimal, gives the factor $g = 1 + r$. A fall has negative $r$. After $n$ steps: $$V_n = V_0 \\, g^n = V_0 (1 + r)^n$$",
      "question": "Which factor describes a fall of 4% a month?",
      "widget": {
        "kind": "choice",
        "layout": "grid",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "right",
            "text": "$0.96$",
            "correct": true
          },
          {
            "id": "sign",
            "text": "$1.04$",
            "why": "You added the 4%. A fall makes $r$ negative: $1 - 0.04$."
          },
          {
            "id": "rate",
            "text": "$0.04$",
            "why": "You wrote the part lost. The factor is the part kept."
          },
          {
            "id": "tenth",
            "text": "$0.6$",
            "why": "You read 4% as 0.4. 4% is 0.04, so the factor is 0.96."
          }
        ]
      },
      "hints": [
        {
          "rung": "nudge",
          "text": "Here $r = -0.04$."
        },
        {
          "rung": "step",
          "text": "$g = 1 + (-0.04) = 0.96$."
        }
      ],
      "feedback": {
        "correct": "$g = 1 - 0.04 = 0.96$.",
        "generic": "Not quite right. Put $r = -0.04$ into $g = 1 + r$."
      },
      "explain": {
        "text": "A fall of 4% has $r = -0.04$, so $g = 0.96$. If $g > 1$ the value grows; if $0 < g < 1$ it decays. With $g = 1$ it stays put."
      }
    },
